**How to implement.** The absorbing half of the noise model moves into `BenchNoise` (001 §Q AT-2; .spec-md §3.23), which makes 001 §T 'From section 10' true: `git grep -n -F "let noisyObserveAbsoluteWith" -- Berreman/BerremanTests/` finds nothing, as every section from S10.2 on asserts. This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples … Migration provided: a move'): after the step exactly one declaration of each moved name exists. Errors are values (AGENTS.md: 'do not throw across a public boundary'): what the harness `failwith`s becomes an `Error` of `MuellerFitError`, and the tests unwrap it with `expectOk`. (1) Into `BenchNoise.fs`, after `misread`: `misreadAbsolute` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:misreadAbsolute`) answering `Result<MuellerMatrix, MuellerFitError>`: the throughput draw FIRST (`trueThroughput * (1.0 + noise.throughput.value * (draws.nextDeviate ()).value)`), then the fifteen element draws in `misread`'s order, each reported element `reportedThroughput * (n.element i j + noise.element.value * (draws.nextDeviate ()).value)` and m₀₀ the reported throughput; a normalization `Error e` is `Error (MuellerNormalizationErr e)`. After `noisyObserveWith`: `noisyObserveAbsoluteWith` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:noisyObserveAbsoluteWith`), the same walk as `noisyObserveWith` with `misreadAbsolute`, answering `Result<MuellerObservation list, MuellerFitError>`. Each moved declaration's doc is cut to its contract in one to three lines (AGENTS.md 'Comments: short, precise, useful'), keeping one line where it guards a hazard the code cannot show. `misreadAbsolute` keeps one line saying the throughput draw comes first so a seed reproduces the experiment (specs/0044/.manual/019-absorbing-biaxial-noisy-tests.md). (2) `InverseFitHarness.fs` deletes both. `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.recoverFromNoisy` pipes `noisyObserveAbsoluteWith forward absorbing noise seed fullConfigurations |> expectOk`. Every consumer opens the product module where the compiler asks and changes nothing else unless named here. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'): the draws are taken in the same order by the same arithmetic. No test is added or removed. The absorbing path is reached by `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests` alone (946 s, its one ensemble fact), so that class is selected here and nowhere else in S10.1, as the S10.1 brief allows for a function reached nowhere else.

**Acceptance.** After the move, `BenchNoise.fs` MUST declare `misreadAbsolute` and `noisyObserveAbsoluteWith` answering `Result`s, `git grep -n -F "let noisyObserveAbsoluteWith" -- Berreman/BerremanTests/` MUST find nothing (001 §T 'From section 10'), and `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests` MUST draw its observations through the product; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the nineteen s33 invariants MUST pass.
